    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/ci-health.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "For ONE commit, zero checks is not a pass",
      "prov:value": "Owner ruling 2026-09-30, bean `52cz`: this is written here so that an agent\nreading PR events **without** the tool knows it too. The tool enforces it\n(`verdictForCommit`, `mergeStateForHead`); this paragraph is for the reader.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 52cz",
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/ci-health.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "`qa-publish` is a job in the gate workflow, and it is not a gate",
      "prov:value": "Since arc `3fva`, `Code quality gates` carries one job that judges nothing:\n`qa-publish`, which runs after `gates` **whatever they concluded** and stores\nthe run's QA results on the orphan `qa-reports` branch (`main/<sha>/` on a\npush, `pr/<n>/<sha>/` on a same-repository PR).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 3fva"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/ci-health.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "`qa-publish` is a job in the gate workflow, and it is not a gate",
      "prov:value": "The owner's merge policy counts it like any job: a PR is handed to the Merge\nSteward only when CI is green on **every** job\n([`continual-progress`](continual-progress.md) §\"Green means handed to the\nMerge Steward\")."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/ci-health.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The report answers about the default branch — and Pages is not on it",
      "prov:value": "**A Pages build outcome is not repository state.** It is a fact GitHub holds\n*about* the repository, and it changes the repository's status without changing\na single byte of it. That is the owner's framing, 2026-09-20, and it settles\nhow the tool must behave: **look external, cache nothing.** A committed answer\nwould be right when it was written and silently wrong from then on, which is\nthe original defect rebuilt in a new place.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/ci-health.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Two more, for the question the three above do not cover",
      "prov:value": "**Crucial exception (bean `folio-assistant-oz5w`)**: staleness is benign\n  only when falling back to an existing live preview,\n  **never when the previous state is a deletion** (where \"stale\" manifests as a\n  404).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean folio-assistant-oz5w"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/ci-health.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The second instance: merge-main's in-place comment",
      "prov:value": "The same edited-in-place doctrine governs `merge-main.yml` (bean `03nl`,\nimplemented by `cat-harness-tools/scripts/merge-main-comment.ts`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 03nl"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/ci-health.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "A superseded PR run is cancelled — and only a PR's",
      "prov:value": "A run on a PR head that a newer push replaced judges a commit nobody will\nmerge, and it still waits for and holds a runner. On 2026-10-05, 16 of the 53\nruns queued in this repository were such runs, and the queue they lengthened\nheld back the fix main's publish was blocked on (#2233). So a workflow that\nruns on `pull_request` declares",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#2233",
        "2026-10-05"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/ci-health.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A green step can be a SKIPPED one: the CI cone",
      "prov:value": "`cat-harness-tools/scripts/ci-cone.ts` (bean `4rbc`, issue #2456) lets a pull request skip a `bun run cat <check>` gate step whose inputs are unchanged since main's last green run.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 4rbc",
        "#2456"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/ci-health.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A green step can be a SKIPPED one: the CI cone",
      "prov:value": "Wire it in when those checks become recordable. Bean `4rbc` records what that takes.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 4rbc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/ci-health.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "A green step can be a SKIPPED one: the CI cone",
      "prov:value": "**The rule it follows: an input set is declared or derived, never inferred.** Owner, 2026-10-07: *\"derived is BEST\"*, then *\"DERIVED = no drift, no extra data fields\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-07"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/ci-health.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Step names describe what the check does, not merely its passing invariant",
      "prov:value": "A CI step named solely after its passing invariant misdescribes any failure\nwhere the check could not run or the baseline was absent (bean `68op`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 68op"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/ci-health.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The accidental-repair trap on derived gates",
      "prov:value": "A green outcome on a derived gate (such as `readme:subgraphs:check`,\n`docs:harness:check`, or other verify/write pairs) must **never be read as\n\"was never broken\"** (bean `folio-assistant-ey1c`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean folio-assistant-ey1c"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/ci-health.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "The accidental-repair trap on derived gates",
      "prov:value": "Observed on 2026-10-03 (three times in two hours on `main`): PR #1938 broke `uploads/README.md`;\nPR #1940 carried a regenerated file and incidentally made `main` green again; then\na direct web-UI upload broke it once more.\n\n**The guard:** The post-merge regeneration pipeline\n(`.github/workflows/post-merge-regen.yml`, `scripts/post-merge-regen.ts`) audits\nderived artefacts after merges to `main` and opens a reviewable repair PR if\nstale.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "PR #1938",
        "PR #1940",
        "2026-10-03"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-03"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
